  m_text: In this example, we demonstrate how Shader Graph can be used to create
    a Custom Lighting model.  Instead of using a Lit Master Stack, we start with
    Unlit and then build all of the lighting calculations using Shader Graph nodes. 
    Because Shader Graph doesn't support loops, we need to use a Custom Function
    node in order to bring in the lighting information and do the math for the additional
    lights in the scene.
